{"slug":"forge-std","fork":"Blockchains/forge-std","upstream":"foundry-rs/forge-std","branch":"master","commit":"c6fa5d82a3a287c4ff23f26c8f7e2958aafd32d9","indexed_at":"2026-10-03T18:35:53Z","category":"dev-tooling","description":"A collection of helpful contracts and libraries for use with Forge and Foundry","readme_summary":"Forge Standard Library is a collection of helpful contracts and libraries for use with Forge and Foundry. It leverages Forge's cheatcodes to make writing tests easier and faster, while improving the UX of cheatcodes. **Learn how to use Forge-Std with the \ud83d\udcd6 Foundry Book (Forge-Std Guide).** This is a helper contract for errors and reverts. In Forge, this contract is particularly helpful for the `expectRevert` cheatcode, as it provides all compiler built-in errors. This is a rather large contract due to all of the overloading to make the UX decent. Primarily, it is a wrapper around the `record` and `accesses` cheatcodes. It can _always_ find and write the storage slot(s) associated with a particular variable without knowing the storage layout. By default, writing to packed storage variables is not supported and will throw an error. However, you can enable packed slot support by calling `en","install_commands":["forge install foundry-rs/forge-std"],"languages_bytes":{"Solidity":1121173,"Python":18121},"file_count":72,"total_bytes":1196416,"licenses":[{"path":"LICENSE-APACHE","detected":"Apache-2.0","head":"Copyright Contributors to Forge Standard Library Apache License Version 2.0, January 2004 http://www.apache.org/licenses/ TERMS AND CONDITIONS FOR USE, REPRODUCTION, AND DISTRIBUTION 1. Definitions. \""},{"path":"LICENSE-MIT","detected":"MIT","head":"Copyright Contributors to Forge Standard Library Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to d"}],"license_spdx_github":"Apache-2.0","spdx_headers":{"MIT OR Apache-2.0":52},"packag